excerpt: "Formation and stability of weak null singularities for the massive and massless Einstein–Vlasov systems without symmetry assumptions, with continuously extendible metrics and bounded Ricci curvature."

abstract: >
  We study the formation and stability of weak null singularities for solutions
  to the massive and massless Einstein–Vlasov systems without symmetry
  assumptions. Extending previous results of Luk in the vacuum setting, we
  establish the existence of spacetimes arising from characteristic initial
  data that develop a singular null boundary while remaining extendible with
  a continuous metric. For both massive and massless particles, the
  energy-momentum tensor and Ricci curvature remain bounded and extend
  continuously to the singular boundary. For genuinely singular initial data,
  the Christoffel symbols in the original double-null coordinates fail to be
  locally square integrable near the boundary. We introduce new commutator
  vector fields that avoid both derivative loss and the most singular
  curvature component. Under additional curvature assumptions, we also prove
  Lipschitz inextendibility across the singular null boundary.
